     c) Convey individual copies of the object code with a copy of the
Corresponding Source on a durable physical medium customarily used for
software interchange; do this occasionally and noncommercially, and
give the recipient a written offer to provide the Corresponding Source
as in 6b above.

     d) Convey the object code by offering access from a designated place
(gratis or for a charge), and offer equivalent access to the
Corresponding Source in the same way through the same place at no
further charge.  You need not require the recipients to copy the
Corresponding Source along with the object code.  If the place to
convey the object code is a network server, the Corresponding Source
may be on a different server (operated by you or a third party) that
supports equivalent access for all of your user's needs.

     e) Convey the object code using peer-to-peer networks, provided
you inform other peers where the Corresponding Source and the object
code are being offered for general access at no charge.

